<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tayfur Sökmen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1892">1892</a>–<a href="/years/1980">1980</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tayfur Sökmen was a Turkish politician who served as head of state of the Hatay State, the short-lived republic formed from the Sanjak of Alexandretta, from 1938 until its annexation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> in 1939. He had long campaigned for the region's union with Turkey and later sat as a deputy for Hatay in the Turkish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tayfur-sokmen.jpg" alt="Tayfur Sökmen" width="180" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tayfur_Ata_S%C3%B6kmen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
